### 관찰, 차용, 비복제, v17 diff

| official source | observed UI structure | borrowed | not copied | v17 screen/component diff |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Buffer Scheduling | New Post opens Composer, channel avatars select destinations, then queue/date/now; scheduled channel posts are edited separately | explicit channel selection, card-level edit, now/schedule decision | default posting action and queue priority, because approval policy must remain visible | Studio header, selected-card bulk bar, card edit/save, SchedulePanel |
| Sprout Message Approval | Compose to Needs Approval, filters, Approval Activity, edit/reject, expired time then reschedule/resubmit | review owner, activity/history, safe expiry recovery | multi-step workflow builder and external approver administration | Approval Inbox, policy CTA, uncertain/repair paths |
| Later Multi-Profile Scheduling | profile checkmarks, Customize X Posts, unsupported profiles greyed out, scheduled posts edited individually | comparison grid, per-channel variant, reason beside disabled action | Access Group terms, ten-profile plan limit and drag-media interaction | TextCardGrid, readiness reason/action, 390 one-column order |
| Later Custom Analytics | period, handle, platform and post-type filters; platform-native definitions | period/account/source/collected time before a next-change claim | cross-platform total, report delivery and plan upsell | Home native metric rows and provider Analytics owners |
| Meta Page insights search excerpt | `Insights > Content > Overview` exposes Page post reach and engagement | Facebook performance remains in selected account owner | Meta shell and uncollected metric values | Facebook owner plus `해당 없음: 미수집` state |

Google OAuth and TikTok Login Kit remain supporting account-identity references, but they are not counted as the product UI benchmark evidence for this retake.

